{"id":"a2-u04","level":"a2","order":4,"title":{"en":"Law and rules","fr":"Le droit et les règles","es":"El derecho y las normas","ar":"القانون والقواعد"},"tip":{"en":"Legal language expresses obligation precisely: \"must\" and \"shall\" for duties, \"may\" for permission, \"must not\" for prohibition. Passive forms are common in rules and contracts.","fr":"Le langage juridique exprime l'obligation avec précision : « doit » pour les devoirs, « peut » pour la permission, « ne doit pas » pour l'interdiction. Le passif est courant dans les règlements et les contrats.","es":"El lenguaje jurídico expresa la obligación con precisión: «deberá» para los deberes, «podrá» para el permiso, «no podrá» para la prohibición. La voz pasiva es frecuente en normas y contratos.","ar":"تعبر اللغة القانونية عن الإلزام بدقة: «يجب» للواجبات و«يجوز» للإذن و«لا يجوز» للمنع. والمبني للمجهول شائع في اللوائح والعقود."},"words":48,"lessons":[{"id":"a2-u04-l1","type":"learn","order":1,"title":{"en":"law, regulation, right","fr":"loi, règlement, droit","es":"ley, reglamento, derecho","ar":"قانون، لائحة، حق"},"count":11},{"id":"a2-u04-l2","type":"learn","order":2,"title":{"en":"judge, lawyer, defendant","fr":"juge, avocat, défendeur","es":"juez, abogado, demandado","ar":"قاض، محام، المدعى عليه"},"count":10},{"id":"a2-u04-l3","type":"learn","order":3,"title":{"en":"verdict, appeal, lawsuit","fr":"verdict, appel, action en justice","es":"veredicto, apelación, demanda judicial","ar":"حكم، استئناف، دعوى قضائية"},"count":11},{"id":"a2-u04-l4","type":"learn","order":4,"title":{"en":"compliance, violation, fine","fr":"conformité, infraction, amende","es":"cumplimiento normativo, infracción, multa","ar":"امتثال، انتهاك، غرامة"},"count":10},{"id":"a2-u04-l5","type":"learn","order":5,"title":{"en":"copyright, jurisdiction, legislation","fr":"droit d'auteur, juridiction, législation","es":"derechos de autor, jurisdicción, legislación","ar":"حقوق النشر، اختصاص قضائي، تشريع"},"count":11},{"id":"a2-u04-l6","type":"learn","order":6,"title":{"en":"damages, claim, settlement","fr":"dommages-intérêts, réclamation, transaction amiable","es":"daños y perjuicios, reclamación, acuerdo extrajudicial","ar":"تعويضات، مطالبة، تسوية"},"count":10},{"id":"a2-u04-l7","type":"learn","order":7,"title":{"en":"privacy, to comply with, to enforce","fr":"vie privée, se conformer à, faire appliquer","es":"privacidad, cumplir con, hacer cumplir","ar":"الخصوصية، يمتثل لـ، ينفذ"},"count":11},{"id":"a2-u04-l8","type":"learn","order":8,"title":{"en":"to appeal, to prohibit, to permit","fr":"faire appel, interdire, autoriser","es":"apelar, prohibir, permitir","ar":"يستأنف، يحظر، يسمح"},"count":10},{"id":"a2-u04-l9","type":"learn","order":9,"title":{"en":"to convict, mandatory, legal","fr":"condamner, obligatoire, légal","es":"condenar, obligatorio, legal","ar":"يدين، إلزامي، قانوني"},"count":10},{"id":"a2-u04-l10","type":"learn","order":10,"title":{"en":"lawful, innocent, guilty","fr":"licite, innocent, coupable","es":"lícito, inocente, culpable","ar":"مشروع، بريء، مذنب"},"count":9},{"id":"a2-u04-l11","type":"story","order":11,"title":{"en":"Conversation","fr":"Conversation","es":"Conversación","ar":"محادثة"},"count":10},{"id":"a2-u04-l12","type":"review","order":12,"title":{"en":"Unit review","fr":"Révision de l'unité","es":"Repaso de la unidad","ar":"مراجعة الوحدة"},"count":10}]}
